{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And he took curd and milk.</b> The Rabbis say: even though he brought bread before them — and if for things he did not tell them he brought before them, for things he did tell them, how much the more so. And even though there is no proof for the matter of eating cheese before meat or meat before cheese, it is a reminder of the matter, as it says: ויקח חמאה וחלב, and afterwards, ובן הבקר." "<b>And a calf.</b> According to Rashi's commentary, he should have written ובני הבקר, but rather this is what it means — immediately, one by one, he prepared it; he brought and served it before them, etc. And it refers to the three calves that he brought. And likewise the interpretation is: each calf that was prepared first, he brought first before them, as stated in [the chapter] HaSocher et HaPoalim." "<b>And they ate.</b> It is found in the Aggadah that they ate, and this is what our Rabbis taught: HaKadosh Baruch Hu said to the angels: a circumcised infant in the house of Israel — he keeps the law more than you, for you ate meat with milk."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:04:39.308559613Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}